  "metadata": {
    "title": "The Hay Wain Bridge",
    "description": "A timber truss bridge across a river, wide enough for the hay wagon. Stone abutments hold up a plank deck, and a Warren truss on each side carries it over the water. The truss is a pony truss, open at the top with nothing overhead, so a hay load of any height clears it. 39 bricks.\n\n## How it is built\n\nEach step is a group in the Editor, so you can select it, delete it or build it again yourself.\n\n1. **River**: four blue Slab 4x4s make an 8x8 stretch of water.\n2. **Abutments**: on each bank, two grey Brick 1x4s turned 90° (press **R**) stand side by side across the road, one high.\n3. **Ramps**: on each side, four grey Shallow Slopes on a grey Plate 2x4 lead from the ground up to the deck. On the east side they are turned 180° so they climb toward the bridge. Together they make a ramp four wide, and the plate lifts its top level with the deck, so a wagon rolls straight on.\n4. **Deck**: three wooden Slab 4x4s in a row, 12 long and 4 wide. The outer two rest half on an abutment, and the middle one spans the river.\n5. **Trusses**: on each side, two Logs lie along the deck edge as the bottom chord and as curbs for the wheels. Four Diagonal Braces stand on them in a /\\/\\ zig-zag (every other one turned 180°), and a Beam across the two peaks makes the top chord.\n6. **Lanterns**: one at each end of the deck, on opposite sides. In World View they light up at night.\n7. **Hay**: two Half Cube bales by the west ramp, dropped off the last load.\n\n## Wide enough for the hay wagon\n\nThe hay wagon is about 2 long and 1.4 wide over its wheels, and it takes up a circle 1.6 across. Between the curbs the road is 3 wide, which leaves 0.7 to spare on each side. Past the trusses the deck and ramps are 4 wide. Nothing crosses over the road, so the hay can be piled as high as it will go.\n\n## Bricks\n\n- River: 4 Slab 4x4\n- Abutments: 4 Brick 1x4\n- Ramps: 8 Shallow Slope 2x1, 2 Plate 2x4\n- Deck: 3 Slab 4x4\n- Trusses: 4 Log, 8 Diagonal Brace 2x2, 2 Beam\n- Lanterns: 2 Lantern\n- Hay: 2 Half Cube\n\n39 bricks in all.",
